OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fbae911f3586c4f7957369244dc2795b582df5cb1109b3b0c6830cb73f60d36f","event_uuid":"830bafa5-5d64-4937-9323-fe27dc512ec7","position":{"commit_sha":"cf8031aa662c0c4af01dccf6dde5385318cc7760","position":"1787027355845885683-830bafa5-5d64-4937-9323-fe27dc512ec7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (2026-08-17): CONFIRMED dynamic root cause. `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:254-267` hard-codes `multiprocessing.get_context(\"fork\")` on every POSIX host; `run_in_worker` reaches it at lines 310-316 and calls `Process.start()`. With one live background thread, runtime tracing observed CPython 3.12 execute `multiprocessing/popen_fork.py:66 -> os.fork()` and emit `DeprecationWarning: This process ... is multi-threaded, use of fork() may lead to deadlocks in the child`. Direct `os.fork()` and direct fork-context Process probes produced the identical warning; a spawn-context probe returned the expected value without warning, ruling out xdist, payload behavior, and generic process creation as causes. The original focused xdist subset passed 47 tests under warning-as-error, so xdist is not a deterministic prerequisite. Compatibility experiment: running the 47-test lifecycle matrix under spawn preserved 46/47 behaviors; only the reap-lag test failed because its fixture mutates the Process with a local unpicklable closure before start. Forkserver was rejected as a drop-in because its Unix-domain control socket conflicts with the unit network guard and the same fixture is unpicklable. Caller sweep found no production caller in-repo, but `run_in_worker` is publicly re-exported at `src/rebar/grounding/__init__.py:40,94`; its current POSIX fork semantics execute arbitrary closures/lambdas, whereas spawn requires picklable/importable callables. Thus the caller-dependency gate requires an explicit callable contract before repair. Recommended contract: fork only in single-threaded hosts; spawn in multithreaded hosts; convert start/pickling failures to the existing fail-open RunResult rather than propagate. Phase 2 remains locked pending behavior approval.","timestamp":1787017564054662001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report after operator approval of the grounding contract.\n\nRoot cause: run_in_worker inherited the platform multiprocessing default. On POSIX/macOS that was fork, which is unsafe once another thread or C-extension state exists; it also hid the serialization contract because closures/lambdas happened to work under fork. The parent boundary only handled a narrow start failure class and did not fail open on result unpickling failures.\n\nRepair: default to multiprocessing.get_context(\"spawn\"); accept an optional caller-owned multiprocessing context; document that default-spawn callables must be module-level/importable and callables/args/kwargs/results must be pickleable, with C-extension state constructed in the child. Process construction/start/serialization and receive/unpickle exceptions now return abstain(other) with spawn-failed or receive-failed detail. Cleanup/reaping remains intact.\n\nHeld-out proof: tests/unit/grounding/test_spawn_contract.py was removed before the fixer worked, then restored unchanged. It passed 4/4: live background thread defaults to spawn; explicit spawn injection works; an unpickleable lambda fails open; a simulated pickle.UnpicklingError on recv fails open. Exact-defect mutation back to fork made 2/4 fail (reported fork and allowed the lambda to complete), then restoration returned GREEN.\n\nReplication/parity: live-thread start-method reproduction returns spawn; existing explicit-fork test proves caller opt-in remains possible. Search found no production run_in_worker callers yet, only the harness/conformance tests, so no existing internal closure caller is broken. Full grounding suite passed 262 tests (the first run had 262 test passes but its isolation postcheck noticed a concurrently created close-gate oracle; rerun initiated with that file present from baseline). make lint and make typecheck pass.","timestamp":1787026211688429001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32098528350\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"failure_type\":\"lint-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"Generated env-var registry drift: src/rebar/grounding/harness.py environment lookup moved from line 55 to 56 while docs/env-vars.md retained the old generated location.\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"Ran scripts/gen_env_registry.py in the patchset worktree and amended docs/env-vars.md; preserved Change-Id and repushed Gerrit 1846 patchset 2.\"],\"retry_count\":1}","timestamp":1787027103837373001}],"created_at":1786914861739893001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4c410eaa-aa6a-4b00-b206-eb89e44e4ed6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc"},{"link_uuid":"9dbd69a7-c0c5-47c9-9778-aaabe3e0e2a1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"},{"link_uuid":"830bafa5-5d64-4937-9323-fe27dc512ec7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"094e-e0be-7522-4e42"}],"description":"## Context\nThe grounding worker harness hard-codes POSIX `fork`. CPython 3.12 warns when this runs in a multithreaded host because the child can deadlock; Python 3.14 no longer defaults to fork. Runtime experiments confirmed `multiprocessing/popen_fork.py -> os.fork()` is the warning source, while spawn preserves 46/47 existing lifecycle tests. The one failure is a test fixture that attaches an unpicklable local closure to a Process. No production caller exists in-repo, but `run_in_worker` is publicly re-exported.\n\n## Approved API contract\n- Default to the cross-platform `spawn` context.\n- Accept an optional caller-supplied multiprocessing context for informed legacy/frozen-executable compatibility; callers explicitly selecting fork own its thread-safety risk.\n- Require worker callables to be importable module-level names and args, kwargs, and return values to be pickleable. Future C-extension bindings construct parser/query state inside the child from plain-data arguments.\n- Preserve the documented never-raise/fail-open contract: process start and pickling failures, plus parent receive/unpickling failures, return an abstaining `RunResult`.\n- Do not add cloudpickle/loky without a demonstrated production caller requiring dynamic callables.\n\n## Plan\n- Add held-out behavioral coverage proving the default worker completes under a live background thread with the fork warning promoted to error.\n- Add contract coverage for explicit context injection and non-pickleable start/receive failures mapping to fail-open results.\n- Switch the default context to spawn, expose optional context injection, and make start/receive cleanup exception-safe.\n- Replace the spawn-incompatible reap-lag test mutation with a parent-only proxy while preserving the crash-vs-timeout oracle.\n- Document the public callable/serialization contract and explicit fork escape hatch.\n- Run the grounding lifecycle/conformance matrix, mutation checks, lint, typecheck, and repository gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Default `run_in_worker` completes under a live background thread with the fork deadlock warning treated as an error.\n- [ ] An explicitly supplied multiprocessing context is used.\n- [ ] Non-importable or non-pickleable worker inputs return `RunResult(abstain_reason=\"other\")` without raising.\n- [ ] Parent receive/unpickling failures return `RunResult(abstain_reason=\"other\")` without raising.\n- [ ] Timeout, large-result drain, exception, signal-crash, cleanup, and reap-lag contracts remain green under spawn.\n- [ ] The documented public contract states importability/pickleability requirements and the explicit fork risk.\n- [ ] Focused grounding tests, lint, typecheck, and repository tests pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/harness.py","reason":"default worker isolation to spawn, expose context injection, and preserve fail-open serialization handling"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py","reason":"cover spawn, explicit context, serialization failures, and spawn-compatible reap lag"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_conformance.py","reason":"verify lifecycle and isolation conformance under the new default context"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document the public worker callable and multiprocessing-context contract"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","094e-e0be-7522-4e42"],["relates_to","9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"39da4e03-26dc-44cd-81d6-69941907ea4f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["warning","grounding","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"5701-5e57-2e94-4b17","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Grounding harness tests fork from multithreaded workers and warn about deadlock risk","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["aebb6f3a-7e55-4898-a74f-b619da4b0cf0","39da4e03-26dc-44cd-81d6-69941907ea4f","4bc71684-2205-4d9e-8b56-6f93086e28ab","e69f5a7f-72e3-4a87-8a1d-275e1b0852fc","9dbd69a7-c0c5-47c9-9778-aaabe3e0e2a1","264a49fb-41ef-4ca6-a7b8-23b28f06b50b","fc956d63-ff02-4e35-9912-9e24a0a9ef0c","c669df10-53fa-412a-963e-2a02408e12ab","03696dc3-bdd3-4c8c-ac46-5a870d136ecc","0c394e63-2347-4821-8012-132892a9d983","830bafa5-5d64-4937-9323-fe27dc512ec7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787027355845885684,"uuid":"1d5c25ce-63c8-42da-b898-a632afe4b4ea"}